* **Why we use it:** Interval notation is a concise way to represent a range of values. The round bracket `(` indicates that the endpoint is not included, while the square bracket `]` indicates that the endpoint is included.\n\n🎯 **Exam Tip:** Always check the inclusion or exclusion of the endpoints. A common mistake is to confuse the brackets, so make sure to double-check whether the endpoints are part of the solution."}
